@20001 = ~Moglus~
@20002 = ~Adventurers? Here? How did you get here?~
    @20003 = ~I used a blue portal in the area where absolute evil resides.~
@20004 = ~A blue portal? Damn, that means it stayed in place after I created it to escape. It should have disappeared on its own.~
    @20005 = ~Escape? What were you trying to escape from?~
    @20006 = ~Well, no, you failed. But I must say that your portal is unstable; it appears and disappears randomly.~
@20007 = ~I escaped from the game room—torture chamber, I should say. I'm hiding here to escape the absolute evil and everything it inflicts on me. I was its familiar, but it delighted in inflicting the worst punishments on me. Well, you get the idea...~
@20008 = ~Damn. That means absolute evil has the ability to find me. I escaped from the game room to escape him and everything he inflicts on me. I was his familiar, but he delighted in inflicting the worst punishments on me. Well, you get the idea.~
	@20009 = ~*Looking around you* and you think that the presence of all these undead is better for you?~
    @200010 = ~Frankly, if absolute evil is that powerful, I doubt that changing location—or plane?—will be enough to keep it from finding you.~
@200011 = ~These undead can't do anything to me. To them, I don't exist. Only the mage can see me, but to her I'm just a zombie bat... and I'm careful not to disabuse her of that notion.~
@200012 = ~Oh, I still have enough power to hide my aura. If he doesn't take the portal, he won't find me. And I doubt he'll take the portal, he's so comfortable on his throne of blood.~
	@200013 = ~And what are you, exactly?~
    @200014 = ~What if he sends his minions? ?~
@200015 = ~I am Moglus, the divine bat.~
@200016 = ~I would know how to hide them. Or I would destroy them. Believe me, I am capable of both.~
    @200017 = ~“Divine”? Isn't that a bit of a pompous name?~
    @200018 = ~So, "Mister". Moglus, what do you propose now?~
@200019 = ~No, it's not. Being the familiar of Absolute Evil has to be earned. You need a certain status for that. And god of bats was the minimum.~
    @200020 = ~Very well. So what do we do now that I've found you?~
@200021 = ~The Bat is silent for a few seconds, then says to you: Listen, I think that if you've made it this far, it's because you're a damn tough bunch. Maybe you can even rid me of Absolute Evil. In that case, rather than going around in circles here, I suggest I accompany you. The material plane surely has plenty to offer a sharp mind like mine. What do you say?~
    @200022 = ~You? In my group? You must be joking?~
    @200023 = ~Why not? What could you possibly offer me?~
	@200024 = ~And I suppose I should expect you to stab me in the back as soon as I turn around?~
@200025 = ~It's not. And I wouldn't take up space in your group. I would follow you from a distance, just enjoying everything your world has to offer.~
@200026 = ~I will follow you from a distance and support you with my magical powers. Ha, and on the prime Material Plane, I am invulnerable. And if something sends me back into the abyss, I will know how to return.~
@200027 = ~Heeer. No. I admit, creatures of the Abyss are given to evil, but not me. I have no evil inclinations, I am only curious. That is what absolute evil cannot bear in me: I did not meet its expectations of murder, domination, and sadism. That is why it tried to destroy me... without success.~
	@200028 = ~All right. Welcome aboard, moglus.~
    @200029 = ~No. I cannot trust a bat from hell. You will stay here.~
@200030 = ~So be it.~
@200031 = ~Sword wraith~		